6. the harness has teeth: the same harness against the scripts as they are at HEAD
================================================================================
$ git show HEAD:scripts/install-retire-debug-keeper.sh > /tmp/zl1-inst-prefix/scripts/...
$ git show HEAD:scripts/install-no-edl-on-panic.sh   > /tmp/zl1-inst-prefix/scripts/...
FAIL  the applier refuses
FAIL  and says what it is leaving alone
FAIL  and names the interface it looked at
FAIL  a build whose gate does not recognise the address that IS there refuses too
FAIL  only the two whose ARGV IS the keeper are matched
pass=123 fail=5

   All five are the SAME defect seen from five sides: section 3's refusal gate never fires (three
   assertions) and section 5's two-keeper match never happens -- because with no address the
   applier dies at line 68 before it can match anything or say anything. Section 4's kill and
   verify assertions PASS against HEAD, which is the honest reading: this was a bug on the
   failure path, not the happy path. A harness that reported 'it never kills' would have been
   describing a different script.

